  "id": "bardetbiedl-syndrome",
  "term": "Bardet–Biedl syndrome",
  "definition": "Bardet–Biedl syndrome is an inherited autosomal recessive disorder marked by a pattern of physical and developmental features that can include retinitis pigmentosa, extra fingers or toes, obesity, intellectual disability, underdeveloped sex organs, kidney dysplasia, and short stature. It is recognized as distinct from Laurence-Moon syndrome.",
